  "question": {
    "text": "Let S be the set of all non - zero real numbers <math><mi>&#945;</mi></math> such that the quadratic equation <math><mi>&#945;</mi><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> has two distinct real roots <math><msub><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>d</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><msub><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> satisfying the inequality <math><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#60;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo></math> Which of the following intervals is(are) a subset(s) of S?",
